EXPERIMENT 2: CASE STUDY OF ARMS PORTAL – POSITIVE TEST SCENARIOS AND TEST CASES

## 1. AIM

To write a case study to identify and analyze the requirements of the ARMS Portal and to prepare positive test scenarios and test cases for the application.

## 2. INTRODUCTION

ARMS Portal is an online application used to manage and access student-related academic information. It allows students to log in, view their profiles, check attendance, access academic results, and perform other academic activities.

The purpose of testing is to verify that all the functions of the portal work correctly when valid inputs are provided.

## 3. REQUIREMENT ANALYSIS

### Functional Requirements

1. User Login: Students should be able to log in using valid credentials.
2. Student Profile: Students should be able to view their personal details.
3. Attendance: Students should be able to check their attendance details.
4. Academic Results: Students should be able to view examination results.
5. Course Details: Students should be able to view registered courses.
6. Fee Details: Students should be able to view fee payment information.
7. Logout: Users should be able to securely log out of the portal.

### Non-Functional Requirements

1. The portal should be user-friendly.
2. The application should respond quickly.
3. User information should be secure.
4. The portal should be available whenever required.
5. The application should work properly on different browsers.

## 4. POSITIVE TEST SCENARIOS

Positive testing verifies whether the application works correctly with valid inputs.

| Scenario ID | Test Scenario |
|---|---|
| TS01 | Verify login using valid username and password. |
| TS02 | Verify that the student dashboard opens successfully. |
| TS03 | Verify that the student profile displays correctly. |
| TS04 | Verify that attendance details are displayed. |
| TS05 | Verify that academic results are displayed. |
| TS06 | Verify that registered course details are displayed. |
| TS07 | Verify that fee payment details are displayed. |
| TS08 | Verify that the user can log out successfully. |

## 5. POSITIVE TEST CASES

| Test Case ID | Test Steps | Test Data | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| TC01 | Open the portal and enter valid login details. Click Login. | Valid username and password | Login should be successful. |
| TC02 | Log in and open the dashboard. | Valid student account | Dashboard should be displayed. |
| TC03 | Open the student profile section. | Valid student account | Student details should be displayed correctly. |
| TC04 | Open the attendance section. | Valid student account | Attendance details should be displayed. |
| TC05 | Open the examination results section. | Valid student account | Academic results should be displayed. |
| TC06 | Open the course details section. | Registered student account | Registered courses should be displayed. |
| TC07 | Open the fee details section. | Valid student account | Fee details and payment status should be displayed. |
| TC08 | Click the Logout button. | Logged-in student account | User should be logged out successfully. |

## 6. SAMPLE TEST INPUTS

- Username: Valid student username
- Password: Valid student password
- Student ID: Valid registered student ID
- Course: Registered course
- Attendance: Available attendance record
- Fee Status: Paid

## 7. EXPECTED OUTPUT

1. The user should log in successfully.
2. The dashboard should open without errors.
3. The student profile should display correct information.
4. Attendance details should be displayed.
5. Examination results should be displayed.
6. Course details should be displayed.
7. Fee payment information should be displayed.
8. Logout should work successfully.

## 8. RESULT

Thus, the requirements of the ARMS Portal were identified and analyzed successfully. Positive test scenarios and test cases were prepared to verify the proper functioning of the application using valid inputs.
